The `LintRule` protocol forces a `fix(self, wiki, results)` signature, but most `fix` implementations don't use `self`. Ruff flags PLR6301 on every one of them.

**Current approach:** Protocol class — all 11 rules must satisfy it but get no shared logic.

**Proposed fix:** Replace with an abstract base class:
```python
class BaseLintRule(ABC):
    @property
    @abstractmethod
    def name(self) -> str: ...
    @property
    @abstractmethod  
    def description(self) -> str: ...
    @abstractmethod
    def check(self, wiki, *, sources_dir=None) -> list[LintResult]: ...
    def fix(self, wiki, results) -> list[LintResult]:
        return results  # default: no-op
```
This gives shared default logic, eliminates PLR6301 warnings, and lets rules override only what they need.

src/knox/output/typst.py guards 'if wiki.metadata and ...';
markdown.py and json_writer.py do not. Models default to {} so this
is unlikely, but the inconsistency is a footgun.
